<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Devanampiya Tissa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Also known as Tissa of Anuradhapura</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Devanampiya Tissa was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anuradhapura">Anuradhapura</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> in the 3rd century BCE and a contemporary and ally of the Maurya emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashoka">Ashoka</a>. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahavamsa">Mahavamsa</a>, the monk Mahinda, Ashoka's son, converted him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a>, and a sapling of the Bodhi tree was planted in Anuradhapura. He founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahavihara">Mahavihara</a> monastery.</p></div>
